{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# MLP Vanilla PINNs: Weak Form — Gaussian Shock\n",
    "\n",
    "**PDE:**\n",
    "$$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\,\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = \\nu\\,\\frac{\\partial^2 u}{\\partial x^2}, \\quad x\\in[0,2\\pi],\\; t\\in[0,T]$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach:** Vanilla PINNs — single network $u_\\theta(t,x)$ over the full domain $[0,T]\\times[0,2\\pi]$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Loss:**\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L} = w_{ic}\\,\\mathcal{L}_{IC} + w_{bc}\\,\\mathcal{L}_{BC} + w_{pde}\\,\\mathcal{L}_{PDE}^{\\text{weak}}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathcal{L}_{PDE}^{\\text{weak}} = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\left(\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N} R(t_i,x_i)\\,v_k(x_i)\\right)^2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** Hopf–Cole analytical solution.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Note on Vanilla PINNs for shocks.**  The vanilla approach samples $(t,x)$ uniformly and trains the network simultaneously across all times.  This violates causality — the network can find solutions that fit $t=0$ but get the evolution wrong.  Equal weighting of IC and PDE losses is critical; a dominant IC weight causes the network to ignore the temporal dynamics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "a0000002",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "torch: 2.10.0+cu128\n",
      "device: cuda\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import sys, os, time\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.getcwd()))\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from scipy.special import erf as sp_erf\n",
    "\n",
    "from pinns_framework import (\n",
    "    PINArchitecture, PINSpatialDimension, PINLossFunction, PINTrainer,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    _trapz = np.trapezoid\n",
    "except AttributeError:\n",
    "    _trapz = np.trapz\n",
    "\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(42)\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "print('torch:', torch.__version__)\n",
    "DEVICE = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else ('mps' if torch.backends.mps.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
    "print('device:', DEVICE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000003",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Gaussian Shock — Exact Solution (Hopf–Cole)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "a0000004",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X0, XF  = 0.0, 2 * np.pi\n",
    "NU_G    = 0.001\n",
    "A_G     = 2.0\n",
    "SIGMA_G = 0.5\n",
    "X0_G    = np.pi\n",
    "T_G     = 3\n",
    "TIMES_G = [3]\n",
    "\n",
    "_sqrt2   = np.sqrt(2.0)\n",
    "_erf_ref = sp_erf(-X0_G / (SIGMA_G * _sqrt2))\n",
    "\n",
    "def gaussian_exact(t, x_arr, nu=NU_G, A=A_G, x0=X0_G, sigma=SIGMA_G):\n",
    "    x_arr = np.asarray(x_arr, dtype=float)\n",
    "    if t == 0:\n",
    "        return A * np.exp(-(x_arr - x0)**2 / (2 * sigma**2))\n",
    "    y    = np.linspace(x0 - 10*sigma, x0 + 10*sigma, 4000)\n",
    "    F_y  = A * sigma * np.sqrt(np.pi/2) * (\n",
    "        sp_erf((y - x0) / (sigma * _sqrt2)) - _erf_ref\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    phi0 = np.exp(-F_y / (2 * nu))\n",
    "    X    = x_arr[:, None]\n",
    "    Y    = y[None, :]\n",
    "    K    = np.exp(-(X - Y)**2 / (4 * nu * t))\n",
    "    dy   = y[1] - y[0]\n",
    "    phi     = (K * phi0).sum(axis=1) * dy\n",
    "    dphi_dx = (-(X - Y) / (2*nu*t) * K * phi0).sum(axis=1) * dy\n",
    "    return -2 * nu * dphi_dx / (phi + 1e-300)\n",
    "\n",
    "x_plot = np.linspace(X0, XF, 500)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "cmap = plt.cm.plasma\n",
    "for i, t in enumerate(TIMES_G):\n",
    "    c = cmap(i / max(len(TIMES_G)-1, 1))\n",
    "    ax.plot(x_plot, gaussian_exact(t, x_plot), color=c, lw=1.8, label=f't={t:.2f}')\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'Gaussian shock — exact  (ν={NU_G}, A={A_G}, σ={SIGMA_G})')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('x'); ax.set_ylabel('u'); ax.legend(fontsize=8, ncol=2); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000005",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. IC / BC"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "a0000006",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "x_ic_np = np.linspace(X0, XF, 400)\n",
    "u_ic_np = gaussian_exact(0, x_ic_np)\n",
    "\n",
    "x_ic = torch.tensor(x_ic_np, dtype=torch.float32).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "u_ic = torch.tensor(u_ic_np, dtype=torch.float32).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "x_bc = torch.tensor([[X0], [XF]], dtype=torch.float32)\n",
    "u_bc = torch.zeros(2, 1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000007",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Architecture and Residual\n",
    "\n",
    "Network input: $(t, x)$ — 2 features.  \n",
    "Architecture: wider and deeper than TD-PINNs because the network must represent the entire space-time solution.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R(t,x) = \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\,\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} - \\nu\\,\\frac{\\partial^2 u}{\\partial x^2}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "a0000008",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "MLP(\n",
      "  (net): Sequential(\n",
      "    (0): Linear(in_features=2, out_features=128, bias=True)\n",
      "    (1): Tanh()\n",
      "    (2): Linear(in_features=128, out_features=128, bias=True)\n",
      "    (3): Tanh()\n",
      "    (4): Linear(in_features=128, out_features=128, bias=True)\n",
      "    (5): Tanh()\n",
      "    (6): Linear(in_features=128, out_features=128, bias=True)\n",
      "    (7): Tanh()\n",
      "    (8): Linear(in_features=128, out_features=1, bias=True)\n",
      "  )\n",
      ")\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Do NOT pass collocation_curvature to Vanilla — that helper calls net(x_spatial)\n",
    "# but the network here expects (t, x) as 2D input, which would give wrong gradients.\n",
    "N_COLLOC = 2000\n",
    "N_TEST   = 80\n",
    "\n",
    "ARCH        = 'MLP'\n",
    "PARAMS_ARCH = {'layers': (2, 128, 128, 128, 128, 1), 'activation': 'tanh'}\n",
    "\n",
    "def burgers_residual(u, t, x, nu):\n",
    "    du_dt  = torch.autograd.grad(u.sum(), t, create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    du_dx  = torch.autograd.grad(u.sum(), x, create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    du_dxx = torch.autograd.grad(du_dx.sum(), x, create_graph=True)[0]\n",
    "    return du_dt + u * du_dx - nu * du_dxx\n",
    "\n",
    "x_dim = PINSpatialDimension('x', domain=(X0, XF), n_colloc=N_COLLOC)\n",
    "print(PINArchitecture(ARCH, PARAMS_ARCH))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000009",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Weak Loss"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "a0000010",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "PINLossFunction(form='weak', dims=['x'], n_test=80, multi_dim_mode='total_degree')\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "loss_weak = PINLossFunction([x_dim], burgers_residual, form='weak', n_test=N_TEST)\n",
    "print(loss_weak)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000011",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Training\n",
    "\n",
    "Weight balance matters a lot for Vanilla PINNs on time-dependent problems:\n",
    "- If `ic_weight` is too large the network locks onto $u_0(x)$ and ignores evolution.\n",
    "- Equal or moderate IC/PDE weighting lets the optimizer actually learn the dynamics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "a0000012",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "=== Gaussian — Vanilla MLP Weak Form ===\n",
      "=== Vanilla PINNs | training over full (t, x) domain ===\n",
      "  [VANILLA] epoch 10000 | loss 3.8857e-05\n",
      "  [VANILLA] epoch 20000 | loss 3.8794e-05\n",
      "Wall time: 66.9 s\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "net = PINArchitecture(ARCH, PARAMS_ARCH)\n",
    "trainer = PINTrainer(\n",
    "    net=net, scheme='VANILLA', loss_fn=loss_weak,\n",
    "    spatial_dims=[x_dim], epochs=20000,\n",
    "    lr=1e-3, tolerance=0,\n",
    "    ic_weight=5.0,    # reduced: was 20 → IC was dominating, killing time evolution\n",
    "    bc_weight=5.0,\n",
    "    pde_weight=5.0,   # equal weight: PDE is as important as IC\n",
    "    verbose=True, log_every=10000,\n",
    "    collocation_fn=None,  # uniform x sampling — curvature fn incompatible with (t,x) net\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=== Gaussian — Vanilla MLP Weak Form ===')\n",
    "t0   = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "nets = trainer.fit(x_ic, u_ic, x_bc, u_bc, T=T_G, nu=NU_G)\n",
    "wall = time.perf_counter() - t0\n",
    "print(f'Wall time: {wall:.1f} s')\n",
    "net_trained = nets[0]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000013",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Solution Plots"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "a0000014",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 400x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dev = trainer.device\n",
    "x_eval_np = np.linspace(X0, XF, 500)\n",
    "\n",
    "def eval_at(net, t_val, x_np):\n",
    "    n   = len(x_np)\n",
    "    t_t = torch.full((n, 1), t_val, dtype=torch.float32, device=dev)\n",
    "    x_t = torch.tensor(x_np, dtype=torch.float32, device=dev).unsqueeze(1)\n",
    "    net.eval()\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        return net(torch.cat([t_t, x_t], dim=1)).cpu().numpy().ravel()\n",
    "\n",
    "sols = {t: eval_at(net_trained, t, x_eval_np) for t in TIMES_G}\n",
    "\n",
    "ncols = len(TIMES_G)\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, ncols, figsize=(4 * ncols, 4), squeeze=False)\n",
    "axes = axes[0]   # always a 1-D array regardless of ncols\n",
    "for ax, t in zip(axes, TIMES_G):\n",
    "    u_ex = gaussian_exact(t, x_eval_np)\n",
    "    ax.plot(x_eval_np, u_ex,     'k-',  lw=2,   label='Exact')\n",
    "    ax.plot(x_eval_np, sols[t],  'r--', lw=1.5, label='MLP Weak')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f't = {t:.2f}', fontsize=10)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('x'); ax.set_ylabel('u'); ax.grid(alpha=0.25)\n",
    "    if t == TIMES_G[0]:\n",
    "        ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "fig.suptitle(f'Gaussian shock (ν={NU_G}) — Vanilla MLP Weak vs Exact', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000015",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Error Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a0000016",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def all_errors(u_pred, u_exact, x):\n",
    "    diff  = np.abs(u_pred - u_exact)\n",
    "    L1    = float(_trapz(diff,        x))\n",
    "    L2    = float(np.sqrt(_trapz(diff**2, x)))\n",
    "    Linf  = float(diff.max())\n",
    "    denom = float(np.sqrt(_trapz(u_exact**2, x))) + 1e-12\n",
    "    return {'L1': L1, 'L2': L2, 'Linf': Linf, 'rel_L2': L2 / denom}\n",
    "\n",
    "rows = []\n",
    "for t in TIMES_G:\n",
    "    u_ex = gaussian_exact(t, x_eval_np)\n",
    "    e    = all_errors(sols[t], u_ex, x_eval_np)\n",
    "    rows.append({'t': t, **e})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_err = pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index('t')\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.float_format', '{:.4e}'.format)\n",
    "print('\\n=== Per-time errors ===')\n",
    "print(df_err.to_string())\n",
    "print('\\n=== Mean ===')\n",
    "print(df_err.mean().to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a0000017",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "t_plot = TIMES_G[1:]\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "for ax, norm in zip(axes, ['L1', 'L2', 'Linf']):\n",
    "    ax.semilogy(t_plot, df_err.loc[t_plot, norm], 'r-o', ms=6)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('t'); ax.set_ylabel(f'{norm} error')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'{norm} error'); ax.grid(True, which='both', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "fig.suptitle('Gaussian shock — Vanilla MLP Weak error evolution', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0000018",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Conservation Diagnostics"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a0000019",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mass_pred, energy_pred, mass_ex, energy_ex = [], [], [], []\n",
    "for t in TIMES_G:\n",
    "    u_p = sols[t]\n",
    "    u_e = gaussian_exact(t, x_eval_np)\n",
    "    mass_pred.append(_trapz(u_p,      x_eval_np))\n",
    "    energy_pred.append(_trapz(u_p**2, x_eval_np))\n",
    "    mass_ex.append(_trapz(u_e,      x_eval_np))\n",
    "    energy_ex.append(_trapz(u_e**2, x_eval_np))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "for ax, vals_ex, vals_w, ylabel, label in [\n",
    "    (axes[0], mass_ex,   mass_pred,   r'$\\int u\\,dx$',   'Mass'),\n",
    "    (axes[1], energy_ex, energy_pred, r'$\\int u^2\\,dx$', 'Energy'),\n",
    "]:\n",
    "    ax.plot(TIMES_G, vals_ex, 'k-',  lw=2,   label='Exact')\n",
    "    ax.plot(TIMES_G, vals_w,  'r-o', lw=1.5, ms=5, label='MLP Weak')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('t'); ax.set_ylabel(ylabel); ax.set_title(label)\n",
    "    ax.legend(); ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "fig.suptitle(f'Gaussian shock (ν={NU_G}) — Conservation', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "cons_rows = []\n",
    "for i, t in enumerate(TIMES_G):\n",
    "    cons_rows.append({'t': t,\n",
    "                      'Δmass':   abs(mass_pred[i]   - mass_ex[i]),\n",
    "                      'Δenergy': abs(energy_pred[i] - energy_ex[i])})\n",
    "print(pd.DataFrame(cons_rows).set_index('t').to_string())"
   ]
  }
 ],
